      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Columbus served as the original Hickman County seat until 1829 when the court moved to Clinton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbus%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town was the northernmost terminus of the Mobile and Ohio Railroad, a line that reached Columbus by 1861.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
